[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/2060229431","html_url":"https://github.com/935963004/LaBraM/issues/13#issuecomment-2060229431","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/13","id":2060229431,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLF0fBs56zJs3","user":{"login":"935963004","id":38138106,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MTM4MTA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38138106?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004","html_url":"https://github.com/935963004","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/935963004/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-04-17T02:33:33Z","updated_at":"2024-04-17T02:33:33Z","body":"Thanks for your interest. Given input data of [batch_size, channels, samples], e.g., [128, 64, 2000], they will be transformed into [batch_size, num_patches, patch_length] in the code, in this example, [128, 640, 200], where we define the patch length as 1 second with sampling rate 200 Hz. Finally, the shape of the output embeddings will be [batch_size, num_patches, embed_dim] as well. In the base model, embed_dim is 200. You can use these embeddings as you need.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/2060229431/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/2060984494","html_url":"https://github.com/935963004/LaBraM/issues/13#issuecomment-2060984494","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/13","id":2060984494,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLF0fBs562CCu","user":{"login":"SamGijsen","id":44772298,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NzcyMjk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44772298?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamGijsen","html_url":"https://github.com/SamGijsen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamGijsen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamGijsen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamGijsen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamGijsen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamGijsen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamGijsen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamGijsen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamGijsen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamGijsen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-04-17T10:55:24Z","updated_at":"2024-04-17T11:42:36Z","body":"Right, but if one aims to obtain crop/epoch-level embeddings then one option would be to average across the patch-dimension (as implemented in self.fc_norm(t.mean(1) as far as I can see), correct? Are these averaged representations also what you used as input for your classification head during finetuning in your paper, which seemed to work well?\r\n\r\nA bit of an unrelated question, but was a seed set for the train:validation split for TUAB? Or some other record of which subjects ultimately constituted your training set?\r\n\r\nAppreciate your help!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions"